    {
      "id": 50,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read this dashboard",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 53,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 7
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Healthy** — consumed and finished track each other, the queue sits near zero,\nretries and dead letters are flat at zero.\n\n**A store is struggling** — retries rise, processing duration's tail stretches\ninto seconds, queue depth grows. Nothing is lost yet: the work is being retried.\n\n**A store stayed down** — retries exhausted and dead letters rise together. Those\nevents are in the dead-letter topic and need a replay once the cause is fixed.\n\n**The consumer is stuck** — *dead-letter publish failed* is above zero. Those\nmessages are in neither the indexes nor the dead-letter topic and are not\ncommitted, so they will arrive again. This is the one line that means data is\ngoing nowhere.\n\n**Backpressure** — arrivals above completions, queue at capacity, memory flat.\nThat is the design working, not an incident.\n\nSettings behind these numbers: `INDEXING_WORKERS`, `INDEXING_QUEUE_SIZE`,\n`KAFKA_RETRY_*`. See `docs/metrics.md` and the retry section of `README.md`."
      },
      "transparent": false
    }
  ]
